     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-AU\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">Hi,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">Not a bug, but I have discovered that the format-changing-output functions differ in whether they tolerate duplicate loci (i.e. gl2..other-data-format functions)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">Specifically gl2genalex gives an error message if you have loci with duplicate names, but for example, gl2structure doesn’t. The error message is slightly cryptic,\r\n but it does point to the number of loci as a problem, and the error disappears if you remove the duplicate loci.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">Of course there shouldn’t be duplicated loci ;-), but some seemed to have slipped through the cracks in one of my datasets, and until I removed them the gl2genalex\r\n function didn’t work.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">It wasn’t too hard to remove the duplicates semi-manually, but I recall that there used to be a function that did it. Would you consider reinstating it?<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">Cheers and Merry Xmas!<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">Olly<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
